    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d532">

                <pb facs="0840" n="818" sameAs="frus:frus1951v02/pg818"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">320/1–2252: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        United States Representative at the United Nations</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Austin</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">confidential</hi>
                        <lb/>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">priority</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1952-01-23T18:17:00-05:00">January 23,
                            1952—6:17 p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    Gadel 808. Re Delga 1143<anchor n="1" xml:id="d532-f1"/> Oatis case. View
                    considerations urtel
                    Dept agrees Del opinion not feasible secure
                    adoption res Oatis case. Sufficient make strong ref Oatis in statement re
                    pertinent Sec ECOSOC Report. However view
                    obvious importance of issue and in absence submission res Dept stresses importance adequate US statement
                    along lines special text of statement re Oatis transmitted to Del by Dept in memo Dec. 11 to Green and
                        Simsarian.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d532-f2"/>
                    Dept still hopes Del able persuade other Dels
                    make appropriate supporting statement.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Acheson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d532-f1" n="1" xml:id="d532-f1-content">
                <p>Dated January 22, <hi rendition="#italic">supra</hi>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d532-f2" n="2" xml:id="d532-f2-content">
                <p>Memorandum not found in Department of State files. James F. Green and James
                    Simsarian were Advisers on the United States Delegation, and both were engaged
                    in Committee Three matters.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
